rts":[[2023,10,8]]}},"container-title":["2023 4th IEEE Global Conference for Advancement in Technology (GCAT)"],"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx7\/10353069\/10353233\/10353543.pdf?arnumber=10353543","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2024,1,12]],"date-time":"2024-01-12T20:52:58Z","timestamp":1705092778000},"score":25.570501,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/ieeexplore.ieee.org\/document\/10353543\/"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,10,6]]},"references-count":30,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/gcat59970.2023.10353543","published":{"date-parts":[[2023,10,6]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,6,10]],"date-time":"2026-06-10T15:29:03Z","timestamp":1781105343320,"version":"3.54.1"},"reference-count":12,"publisher":"IGI Global","isbn-type":[{"value":"9781668463031","type":"print"},{"value":"9781668463048","type":"electronic"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2022,6,10]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>A Bag-of-Words model is widely used to extract the features from text, which is given as input to machine learning algorithm like MLP, neural network. The dataset considered is movie reviews with both positive and negative comments further converted to Bag-of-Words model. Then the Bag-of-Word model of the dataset is converted into vector representation which corresponds to a number of words in the vocabulary. Each word in the review documents is assigned with a score and the scores are later represented in vector representation which is later fed as input to neural model. In the Kera's deep learning library, the neural models will be simple feedforward network models with fully connected layers called \u2018Dense'. Bigram language models are developed to classify encoded documents as either positive or negative. At first, reviews are converted to lines of token and then encoded to bag-of-words model. Finally, a neural model is developed to score bigram of words with word scoring modes.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.4018\/978-1-6684-6303-1.ch034","type":"book-chapter","created":{"date-parts":[[2022,7,22]],"date-time":"2022-07-22T12:53:48Z","timestamp":1658494428000},"page":"619-636","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Develop a Neural Model to Score Bigram of Words Using Bag-of-Words Model for Sentiment Analysis"],"prefix":"10.4018","author":[{"given":"Anumeera","family":"Balamurali","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"St.Joseph's College of Engineering, India"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Balamurali","family":"Ananthanarayanan","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Tamilnadu Agriculture Department, India"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"2432","reference":[{"key":"978-1-6684-6303-1.ch034.-1","unstructured":"Barry, J. (2016). Sentiment analysis of online reviews using bag-of-words and LSTM approaches. Google Tech Report. A. Suresh Babu and P. N. V. S."},{"key":"978-1-6684-6303-1.ch034.-2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.18653\/v1\/W18-0911"},{"key":"978-1-6684-6303-1.ch034.-3","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"Brownlee, J. (2017). Deep learning for natural language processing. Machine learning mastery. Edition: v1.1","DOI":"10.1007\/978-1-4842-3733-5_1"},{"key":"978-1-6684-6303-1.ch034.-4","unstructured":"Chelba, C., Norouzi, M., & Bengio, S. (2017, June 20). N-gram language modelling using recurrent neural network estimation. arXiv:1703.10724v2 [cs.CL]. Google Tech Report"},{"key":"978-1-6684-6303-1.ch034.-5","unstructured":"Cole, R. A., Yan, Y., & Bailey, T. (2001). The influence of bigram constraints on word recognition by humans: Implications for computer speech recognition. ARPA HLT meeting."},{"key":"978-1-6684-6303-1.ch034.-6","first-page":"2493","article-title":"Natural language processing (almost) from scratch.","author":"Collobert","year":"2011